Using square brackets for a collection initializer is invalid in C#. Replace this with a valid initializer such as: return new List<OpenApiServer> { new OpenApiServer { Url = serverUrl } };
```suggestion
            return new List<OpenApiServer> { new OpenApiServer { Url = serverUrl } };
```

The syntax '[.. addresses.Select(...)]' is not valid in C#. Consider converting the enumerable to a list with a valid collection initializer, for example: return addresses.Select(address => new OpenApiServer { Url = address }).ToList();
```suggestion
            return addresses.Select(address => new OpenApiServer { Url = address }).ToList();
        }
        return new List<OpenApiServer>();
```
